    "label": "P1: Text 1 - Question B",
    "q": "Question B (50 marks):\nYou are the captain of a school's sports team, about to compete as the underdogs in the final of a national competition. Write the text of the pre-match team-talk you would deliver.\n\nMust include:\n- Outline aspects of the game plan you'll employ on the field\n- Remind them of the strengths and weaknesses of your opponents\n- Motivate them to overcome the odds and achieve victory",
    "a": "Sample Opening:\n\"Listen up, team. Gather round. I know what everyone's been saying all week - we're the underdogs. We shouldn't even be here. They've got the bigger budget, the fancier facilities, the star players everyone's heard of. But you know what? That's exactly why we're going to win today...\"\n\nStructure Tips:\n1. Acknowledge underdog status - Show you understand the challenge but reframe it as an advantage (no pressure, element of surprise, motivation).\n2. Game plan specifics - Describe actual tactics: \"We'll press high in the first 20 minutes while they're overconfident... focus on quick transitions... exploit their weak left side...\"\n3. Opponent analysis - \"Their striker is fast but predictable - always cuts inside. Their defense is solid but slow to turn. They expect us to sit back - we won't.\"\n4. Emotional appeal - Reference shared struggles, past victories, belief in each other. Use \"we\" language. Build to crescendo.\n5. Call to action - End with specific, actionable instruction and rallying cry: \"So when that whistle blows, we hit them with everything we've got. Are you ready?\""
