    "label": "P1: Text 2 - Question B",
    "q": "Question B (50 marks):\nYou are a hotel manager. A recent, disgruntled guest has left a highly critical review on a travel-review website. Write your online response.\n\nMust include:\n- Outline the proud tradition and history of your establishment\n- Challenge the specific criticisms of the guest reviewer\n- Encourage the reviewer to return by highlighting upcoming events in your hotel and its locality",
    "a": "Sample Structure:\n\nOpening: Thank them for feedback (professional tone), acknowledge their disappointment, introduce hotel history naturally.\n\nHistory: \"The Grand Harbour Hotel has welcomed guests since 1887, earning our reputation through...\" - brief but proud, not defensive.\n\nAddress Criticisms: Be specific. If they complained about noise: \"I was surprised to read about noise disturbance as our rooms were renovated in 2023 with soundproofing...\" Challenge factually, not emotionally.\n\nInvite Return: \"I would love the opportunity to restore your faith in our service. This summer we're hosting...\" - list specific events, special offers, local attractions.\n\nTone: Professional, courteous, confident but not arrogant. Acknowledge without groveling. Focus on solutions."
