    "label": "P1: Text 3 - Planet Earth from Space",
    "q": "Paper 1 - Text 3: Planet Earth from Space (50 marks)\nSource: Extracts from Samantha Harvey's novel \"Orbital\" (2024)\nTheme: Six astronauts in a spacecraft observe Earth from space - perspective shift from viewing the planet from outside.\n\nKey Points from Text 3:\n- Setting: H-shaped spacecraft, six astronauts (American, Japanese, British, Italian, two Russian), orbiting Earth, nine-month mission.\n- Initial Attraction: Night views - \"gorgeous encrusting of city lights\", \"thick embroidered urban tapestries\", electric excess. Can point to home cities.\n- Perspective Shift: \"After a week or so\" they come to love the daytime earth - \"humanless simplicity of land and sea\", \"the way the planet seems to breathe, an animal unto itself.\"\n- Key Imagery: Earth as mother (\"Mother Earth... waiting for her children to return\"), as lover (\"exulted lover\"), as miracle (\"suspended jewel so bright\").\n- Unity Message: At night, only ONE man-made border visible (Pakistan-India). \"By day even that has gone.\" Shows Earth's natural unity despite human divisions.\n- Emotional Response: \"A desire takes hold... the need (fuelled by fervour) - to protect this huge yet tiny earth.\" Seeing Earth's fragility inspires protective instinct.\n- Future Perspective: Roman contemplates space station ending through \"restless spirit of endeavour\" - \"Striking out, further and deeper. The moon, Mars.\" Human nature: \"not made to stand still.\"",
    "a": "Question B (50 marks):\nQ: You are a contributor to a podcast entitled \"Eyes Wide Open\" where you reflect on how your perspective on a significant issue changed as a result of an experience or encounter.\n\nMust include:\n- Identify the issue and explain your previous attitude towards it\n- Describe the experience or encounter that changed your perspective\n- Consider some of the life lessons that you and others can learn from this reflection\n\nSample Structure:\n\nOpening: \"Welcome back to Eyes Wide Open. I'm [name], and today I want to talk about the moment I realized...\" - podcast tone, conversational.\n\nThe Issue: Choose something meaningful - climate change, homelessness, mental health, immigration, technology addiction. State your previous view clearly: \"I used to think... I believed... My attitude was...\"\n\nThe Experience: Tell the story vividly. Use sensory details. Build to the moment of realization. \"That's when it hit me...\" Make it personal and specific.\n\nLife Lessons: Extract broader wisdom: \"What I learned is...\", \"The lesson here is...\", \"If there's one thing listeners can take away...\" Connect personal experience to universal truths.\n\nClosing: \"So that's my story. Thanks for listening to Eyes Wide Open. I'd love to hear about your perspective-changing moments...\" - podcast sign-off."
